brief:
Execute the approved ralplan consensus plan at .gjc/plans/ralplan/2026-06-09-0408-43ad/pending-approval.md for the remaining undone work on agentdir GitHub issues #18 and #19. Branch dev. Constraints: research/docs + non-destructive CI dry-run gates only; NO mount-driver/FUSE/ProjFS/WinFsp implementation; NO real publish (cargo publish / npm publish / npm pack / maturin must not run locally); checks stay zero-dependency stdlib; reuse crates/agentdir/tests/issue_18_release_qa.py conventions.

@goal: Document zero-copy read-only view feasibility and decision (#19)
Create docs/zero-copy-readonly-views.md satisfying all four issue #19 acceptance criteria: (a) per-platform approaches with privileges/deployment — Linux read-only bind mount + FUSE passthrough, Windows ProjFS + WinFsp, macOS APFS reflink (already implemented); (b) recommended default per platform; (c) explicit per-mechanism verdict on normal-file compatibility WITHOUT copying data, including that a read-only bind mount cannot produce agentdir's arbitrary restructured virtual tree without an overlay/FUSE layer, and that CoW reflink is filesystem-level (APFS/Btrfs/XFS) not macOS-only; (d) a Decision section opening with ONE unambiguous verdict sentence (remain a documented limitation vs start an implementation project) followed by trigger conditions and ADR fields. Then reconcile AGENTS.md "Future / Out of Current Scope" to link the new doc with no contradictory claims. Verify with the plan's grep checklist (test -f, bind mount, FUSE, ProjFS+WinFsp, reflink, "## Recommended default per platform", "## Decision", AGENTS.md link).

@goal: Add release-workflow dry-run gates (#18 residual)
Add `cargo publish -p agentdir-cli --dry-run` to .github/workflows/release-rust.yml as a step placed AFTER the "Wait for crates.io sparse index" step and BEFORE the "Publish agentdir-cli" step. Add `npm pack --dry-run` to .github/workflows/release-node.yml (working-directory bindings/node) as a step BEFORE the "Publish" (npm publish) step. Extend crates/agentdir/tests/issue_18_release_qa.py with two zero-dependency stdlib contains-checks: test_release_rust_workflow_dry_runs_cli_before_publish (asserts the rust dry-run string present) and test_release_node_workflow_packs_before_publish (asserts the npm pack dry-run string present). Verify: grep both YAML files; python3 crates/agentdir/tests/issue_18_release_qa.py exits 0 with all PASS; make test and make lint unaffected. Do NOT execute any real publish/pack/maturin command.
